# BHLabs — lab tests in OCL

Source: `bandahealth/BHLabs`  
UI: https://app.openconceptlab.org/#/orgs/bandahealth/sources/BHLabs/  
Canonical example: concept `2` (Urine microscopy panel) in `external-mocks/files/ocl/BHLabs-concepts.json`

## Concept types

| Type | concept_class | datatype | When |
|------|---------------|----------|------|
| Panel | `LabSet` | `None` | Groups related tests (e.g. urine microscopy panel) |
| Individual test | `Test` | `Numeric`, `Coded`, `Text`, etc. | Standalone orderable test |
| Drug (C&S antibiotics) | `Drug` | `Coded` | Rare; use `PANEL_1`, `PANEL_2` extras for specimen panels |

## Mapping types

- **CONCEPT-SET** — panel → member test. `from_concept_url` is the panel; `to_concept_url` is the child (CIEL or LOINC).
- **SAME-AS** — BHLabs concept equivalent to an external concept (often the panel itself mapped to CIEL).

Do not use SAME-AS where CONCEPT-SET is intended (panel membership).

## Mapping extras (on CONCEPT-SET)

- `local_name` — short label shown in MOH-706 and UI (e.g. `"Urine T. Vaginalis"`)
- `MOH-706` — numeric line position on MOH 706 form (e.g. `1.1`, `1.8`)

## Concept extras

- `local_name` — friendly display name on the concept itself when different from the formal name

## External targets

- **CIEL**: `to_source_url: /orgs/CIEL/sources/CIEL/`, `to_concept_code: "{id}"`
- **LOINC**: `to_source_url: /orgs/Regenstrief/sources/LOINC/`, `to_concept_code: "{loinc}"`

Verify the external concept name before mapping.

## API upload pattern

```json
POST /orgs/bandahealth/sources/BHLabs/concepts/
{
  "concept_class": "LabSet",
  "datatype": "None",
  "names": [{ "name": "...", "locale": "en", "locale_preferred": true, "name_type": "Fully Specified" }],
  "extras": { "local_name": "..." }
}

POST /orgs/bandahealth/sources/BHLabs/mappings/
{
  "map_type": "CONCEPT-SET",
  "from_concept_url": "/orgs/bandahealth/sources/BHLabs/concepts/{panel_id}/",
  "to_concept_url": "/orgs/CIEL/sources/CIEL/concepts/{child_id}/",
  "extras": { "local_name": "...", "MOH-706": 1.1 }
}
```

## Workflow checklist

1. Create or locate the panel concept (`LabSet`)
2. Create or locate each member test concept
3. Add CONCEPT-SET mappings panel → members with `local_name` and `MOH-706`
4. Add SAME-AS on the panel if it maps to a CIEL panel concept
5. Verify in OCL UI; run Concept Sync with `source=BHLabs`
